# COPIED-METHOD-DECLARED-FORMAL, two classes of formation with two receiving spaces: run's formal g receives getr
# through b1, a copy (the copy's own occurrence), and the unit's getq; getq reads the free name bonus and getr does
# not, so they are formed differently, and getr's class comes first.  The class of the occurrence g holds is chosen
# before the actuals by the child its holder keeps at the method's slot -- the copy's getr is getr's class though no
# unit address is its address -- and each class admits w in its occurrence's space.  HEAD compared with the unit's
# occurrences only and ran the copy's getr as the remaining class.  41 and 403.  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
Wide:
    int: pad 9
    int: x 2
end: Wide
int: bonus 3
int: tag 1
fn: getr (Wide: q) int
    return: q\x * 10 + node\tag
end: getr
fn: getq (Wide: q) int
    return: q\x * 100 + bonus
end: getq
Box:
    int: v 0
    fn: getr
end: Box
fn: run (getq: g; Wide: w) int
    return: g(w)
end: run
b1: merge: Box
w: merge: Wide
w\x: 4
tag: 5
int: r run(b1\getr; w)
int: s run(getq; w)
int: ok 7
if: r != 41 || s != 403
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
